{
  "_note": "The refining chain: dig face -> ore -> smelter (needs coal + power) -> ingots -> workshop -> components. Every recipe names a building, a power draw and a labour cost, because a recipe with only inputs and outputs cannot express why the smelter stops when the grid browns out. Note there is deliberately NO recipe producing scrubber-catalyst.",
  "recipes": [
    {
      "id": "smelt-steel",
      "building": "smelter",
      "stage": 1,
      "inputs": [{ "id": "iron-ore", "qty": 2 }, { "id": "coal", "qty": 1 }],
      "outputs": [{ "id": "steel-billet", "qty": 1 }],
      "powerDraw": 40,
      "labour": 2,
      "ticks": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "draw-copper-wire",
      "building": "smelter",
      "stage": 1,
      "inputs": [{ "id": "copper-ore", "qty": 2 }, { "id": "coal", "qty": 1 }],
      "outputs": [{ "id": "copper-wire", "qty": 1 }],
      "powerDraw": 35,
      "labour": 2,
      "ticks": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "coke-coal",
      "building": "smelter",
      "stage": 1,
      "inputs": [{ "id": "coal", "qty": 2 }],
      "outputs": [{ "id": "fuel", "qty": 1 }, { "id": "activated-carbon", "qty": 1 }],
      "powerDraw": 25,
      "labour": 1,
      "ticks": 4,
      "_note": "One process, two outputs — burning coal for heat and baking it for filter media are the same oven. This is what couples Air to Mechanical."
    },
    {
      "id": "refine-precision-contacts",
